# app-ads.txt template for https://huntertrgy.github.io/app-ads.txt
# NOT LIVE: this file is an example. Do not publish an app-ads.txt with a placeholder id.
#
# How to fill it (docs/legal/README-publishing.md section 3):
#  1. AdMob -> Apps -> View all apps -> "app-ads.txt" -> "How to set up app-ads.txt", or
#     AdMob -> Settings -> Account information -> Publisher ID (looks like pub-1234567890123456).
#  2. Save it as app-ads.txt at the ROOT of the separate user-site repo
#     Huntertrgy/Huntertrgy.github.io (not in site/: this project site is served under
#     /willowbrew-privacy/ and cannot answer /app-ads.txt). Replace pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX with
#     your publisher id and keep the rest of the line exactly:
#     google.com, <pub id>, DIRECT, f08c47fec0942fa0
#  3. Push that repo; check https://huntertrgy.github.io/app-ads.txt shows the line
#     (plain text, root of the host, HTTP 200, no redirect).
#  4. The Play listing's Website field stays https://huntertrgy.github.io/willowbrew-privacy/ :
#     AdMob looks for app-ads.txt at the root of that host. It crawls after the app is
#     published and linked in AdMob (24-72 h).
#  Runbook: production/release/publish-legal-site.md section 5.
google.com, pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX, DIRECT, f08c47fec0942fa0
